# TSan suppressions for the proof-check runs on C (ceaa1101d) plus northstar/proof-checks.
# Every entry is a report class outside the lane phases and the phase barrier; none is suppressed on
# the write-lane, replica-apply or MAINT paths. Classes refer to sanitizers/sanitizers.md (S1 run).
#
# K1 Object header word (design section 9, LOW): the fast GET's LFU touch CASes the 32-bit header word
#    on an IO thread while another thread reads the type bits of the same word plainly
#    (objectGetType). READ phase only; the CAS never changes the type bits. 8 reports.
race:fastGetTouch
# K2 Forkless save thread vs main: INFO reads the iterator status, CONFIG SET writes a config the saver
#    reads (rdbSaveKeyValuePair). Stock forkless-save code, not a lane. 5 reports.
race:bgIteratorGetStatus
race:returnCurrentItemToMainThread
race:rdbSaveKeyValuePair
# G11 Crash-report thread sampler runs a callback in a signal handler (stock). 2 reports.
race:invoke_callback
signal:invoke_callback
# G3/G7/G8 Stock IO-thread handoffs: the client flags word and the postpone-update-state bit written
#    after the job publish; the event loop's dont-wait bit read by the poll offload; the io_read_state
#    byte stored plainly by ioThreadWriteSlab and read by sendReadToIOThreads (G5/G6). 5 reports.
race:ioThreadReadQueryFromClient
race:readToQueryBuf
race:connSetPostponeUpdateState
race:aeSetDontWait
race:ioThreadWriteSlab
race:sendReadToIOThreads
# G2 Lock order: createIOThread takes io_threads_mutex under the module GIL at start-up. 2 reports.
deadlock:createIOThread
deadlock:moduleAcquireGIL
